From: Emilien <4016501+unixfox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:32:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=E2=9C=A8=20feat(chat):=20run=20the=20agent's?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20tools=20on=20the=20server=20for=20native=20mobile=20clients?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The native LobeHub apps stream `/webapi/chat` without tool definitions and
have no tool loop, so agents with MCP connectors silently lose their tools
on mobile (#19017).

For a native mobile conversation turn (app user agent + `Conversation`
trace naming the agent and topic), the chat endpoint now resolves the
agent's enabled, server-executable tools through the existing discovery
pipeline, runs the model → tool → model loop on the server and streams a
plain completion back. Tool calls never reach the client, approval-gated
calls are refused instead of auto-approved, and the client keeps owning
message persistence. Every other request is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
